								<div class="title" id="post-title-4413839">
																		SCP-4581: The &quot;Anti-Racist Audiocassette&quot;
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tsercele" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2891035); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2891035&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200901" alt="Tsercele" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2891035)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tsercele" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2891035); return false;" >Tsercele</a></span> <span class="odate time_1572791117 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Nov 2019 14:25</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4413839">
									

<p>It's my first SCP! I've been reading the wiki for a long time and I'm thrilled to finally contribute. Many thanks go out to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573428852" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;">cybersqyd</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5255688); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5255688&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573428852" alt="DrAkimoto" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5255688)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drakimoto" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5255688); return false;">DrAkimoto</a></span> for providing detailed feedback and greenlighting my concept, and to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1345012&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573428852" alt="kinchtheknifeblade" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1345012)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kinchtheknifeblade" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1345012); return false;">kinchtheknifeblade</a></span> - for taking an early look, and for developing such a fun GoI!</p>
<p><strong>A peek behind the curtain</strong>: A few months ago, I heard that someone had used copyrighted music to stymie a would-be propagandist, and I thought that was a brilliant nonviolent solution. Eventually, I realized that was the same kind of thing Gamers Against Weed would appreciate, and I started thinking about delivery media. I've always loved the audacious visual design of <em>In God We Trust, Inc.</em>, and this seemed like an obvious match&#8230; particularly when I realized the younger members of GAW would inevitably clown on its creator for being behind the times. The character of &quot;steakshift&quot; emerged from the ensuing back-and-forth.</p>
<p>There are a few deliberate themes in this piece: the omnipresence of the observer effect, culture clash, the fuzzy definition of &quot;non-violence&quot;, and the inevitable ripple effect of all human action. Like many anomalies, this one does <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/things-what-do-a-thing-an-essay-on-things">exactly what the designer intended</a>&#8230; just a <em>bit too well</em>.</p>
<p>There's a few niche references scattered through this piece (the Tipper Gore joke being most obvious). I wonder if people will spot them?</p>
<p><strong>Attributions</strong>: The cassette image is composited from three different CC assets:</p>
<ul>
<li>Base: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unlabelled_audio_cassette.jpg">Ubcule's retouched compact cassette (CC 0)</a>;</li>
<li>Detail: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Compactcassette.jpg">Thegreenj's compact cassette (CC 2.5/ CC 3)</a>;</li>
<li>Logo: <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anti-racist-flag_(v).svg">Tankist-777's anti-racist flag (CC 0)</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>I used <a href="https://github.com/alexadam/img-encode">alexadam's img-encode program</a> to write the &quot;Stephen King, hit by car&quot; joke onto an audio spectrogram.</p>
<p>Also, credit where it's due: the &quot;MxMasters&quot; alias is inspired by one of <a href="https://twitter.com/mcclure111/status/722962790470803456">@mcclure111's jokes on Twitter</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Update</strong>: SCP-4581 now has an accompanying Tale, set in the immediate aftermath of steakshift's interrogation! I hope you enjoy stoners riffing on movie footage, and also deep emotional turmoil: <strong>&quot;<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/smile-you-are-being-watched">Smile! You Are Being Watched!</a>&quot;</strong></p>

							</div>

								
